at a distance you could mistake hi-rez  Studios game paladin's for overwatch  there are a few similar character  designs and abilities in both games  leading some internet commenters to call  paladins a clone high res CEO Todd  Harris addressed these accusations in a  lengthy reddit post and in an interview  with IGN while he admits paladin's  borrowed some mechanics like kill cams  and lag compensation he fully denies the  game being a ripoff he responded while  overwatch is a fine game it was not the  inspiration for paladins for the hero  shooter genre the game that deserves the  most credit is Team Fortress 2 we  released a tf2 inspired class-based  shooter called Global Agenda way back in  2010 paladins was conceived as a fantasy  version of global agenda and of the  approximately 85 combat abilities  currently in paladins the vast majority  are from the game we made 10 years ago  Paris's reddit post contains plenty of  links to paladins footage that predates  overwatch in the end this whole debacle  seems like a classic case of parallel  thought of course if you want to avoid  the issue altogether  you could always play high reza's  mythological mobis might instead and to  keep up with all the upcoming projects  from both high-res and blizzard you're  already in the right place
 

